{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2025-54771","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"A use-after-free vulnerability has been identified in the GNU GRUB (Grand Unified Bootloader). The flaw occurs because the file-closing process incorrectly retains a memory pointer, leaving an invalid reference to a f…","description":"A use-after-free vulnerability has been identified in the GNU GRUB (Grand Unified Bootloader). The flaw occurs because the file-closing process incorrectly retains a memory pointer, leaving an invalid reference to a file system structure. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to cause grub to crash, leading to a Denial of Service. Possible data integrity or confidentiality compromise is not discarded.","published":"2025-11-18T18:20:40.350Z","lastModified":"2026-09-01T11:53:34.202Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"MEDIUM","cvss":4.9},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":{"vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L","baseScore":4.9,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"},"v4_0":null},"cwe":[{"cweId":"CWE-825","name":"Expired Pointer Dereference","source":"cve.org"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"GNU","product":"grub2","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":null,"status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"2.14"}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10","versions":[],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:7","versions":[],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8","versions":[],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:9","versions":[],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4","cpe":"cpe:/a:redhat:openshift:4","versions":[],"platforms":[]},