{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2025-61661","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"A vulnerability has been identified in the GRUB (Grand Unified Bootloader) component. This flaw occurs because the bootloader mishandles string conversion when reading information from a USB device, allowing an attack…","description":"A vulnerability has been identified in the GRUB (Grand Unified Bootloader) component. This flaw occurs because the bootloader mishandles string conversion when reading information from a USB device, allowing an attacker to exploit inconsistent length values. A local attacker can connect a maliciously configured USB device during the boot sequence to trigger this issue. A successful exploitation may lead GRUB to crash, leading to a Denial of Service. Data corruption may be also possible, although given the complexity of the exploit the impact is most likely limited.","published":"2025-11-18T18:20:42.151Z","lastModified":"2026-09-01T11:53:52.929Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"MEDIUM","cvss":4.8},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":{"vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:P/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H","baseScore":4.8,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"},"v4_0":null},"cwe":[{"cweId":"CWE-131","name":"Incorrect Calculation of Buffer Size","source":"cve.org"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"GNU","product":"grub2","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":null,"status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"2.14"}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10","versions":[],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:7","versions":[],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8","versions":[],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux